<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>And then at the moment my heart turns to Thee,</l><l>The eyes of my spirit Your presence can see;</l><l>While all is so fresh and the sunlight breaks through—</l><l>My cup runneth over with joy!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>And when at the noontime I’m hungry and worn</l><l>And feel that the cares of this world have me torn,</l><l>You come as my haven, my rest, and my food—</l><l>My cup runneth over with joy!</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>And then in the evening when my thoughts are free,</l><l>Remembr’ing that You, Lord, still dwell within me,</l><l>This sweet fact releases a river in me—</l><l>My cup runneth over with joy!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
